{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ותרומת ידך", :translit "u'trumat yadekha", :gloss "and the terumah of your hand"} {:he "לפני ה'", :translit "lifnei Hashem", :gloss "before Hashem"} {:he "כי תרומת ידך היינו ביכורים", :translit "ki terumat yadekha hainu bikkurim", :gloss "for the terumah of your hand — that is first fruits"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent-verse reading: תרומת ידך in v.17 parsed through the eating-context of the preceding phrase לפני ה'"}], :frame {:text "The term תרומת ידך appears in the list of sacred portions that must be consumed 'before the LORD' in the central sanctuary (Deuteronomy 12:17). The phrase לפני ה' in the immediately preceding verse (Deuteronomy 12:18) establishes the consumption context, and Ba'al HaTurim reads תרומת ידך as referring specifically to ביכורים, first fruits, which Deuteronomy 26:1–11 requires to be brought and eaten in that setting.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 12:17" "Deuteronomy 12:18" "Deuteronomy 26:1-11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent-verse reading: תרומת ידך in v.17 parsed through the eating-context of the preceding phrase לפני ה'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:12.604366108Z", :model "glm-5.2"}